Title Management of postpartum DVT in a breastfeeding woman
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Obstetrics > Medical complications in pregnancy
CO Flag as important Notes
A 31-year-old woman develops deep vein thrombosis (DVT) one week after delivery. She is
started on enoxaparin. You are planning to start her on warfarin on discharge, but the mother
is reluctant to take warfarin because she wants to breastfeed her baby and she thinks that
