Title Management of a painful vulvar lesion in a 25-year-old man
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Gynecology > Disorders of the vulva
(Flag as important
A 25-year-old female presents with pain and swelling of her vulva. She has been experiencing
discomfort during sexual intercourse and while walking for the past few days. She denies any
history of sexually transmitted infections. Her partner is asymptomatic. She is afebrile and
generally well. On pelvic examination, a red, hot swelling is noted in the posterior end of the
labia majora. Speculum exam reveals normal appearing mucosa without significant discharge.
