Question ID 531
Title Diagnosing the cause of postpartum fever in a 27-year-old woman
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Obstetrics > Postpartum issues
CO Flag as important Notes
A 27-year-old woman presents to the hospital''s emergency department after giving birth to a
healthy male baby four days ago with a complaint of fever. During the vaginal delivery, she
sustained a small vaginal laceration. The lesion was small and did not require sutures for repair.
