Title Diagnosing the cause and management of infertility in a 32-year-old woman
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Gynecology > Infertility
© Flag as important Notes
A 32-year-old woman presents to your clinic for advice. She has been married for the past 2
years and has not been able to conceive. Blood tests show the following results:
® Luteinizing hormone (LH): 1 U/L (3-16)
® Follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH): 0.5 U/L (2 - 8)
© Thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH): 0.3 mU/L (0.5 -5)
® Prolactin: 8750 U/L (<600 U/L)
