Question
427
Diagnosing the cause of vaginal bleeding and abdominal cramps in a 12-week pregnant
woman
Obstetrics / Gynecology > Obstetrics > Failed pregnancy
A 21-year-old woman, G1P0, comes to your clinic at 12 weeks of pregnancy. She has been
complaining of mild vaginal bleeding for the past 12 hours, associated with bouts of mild
cramping and lower abdominal pain. On vaginal examination, the cervical os is closed, and
