QuestionID 191
Title Initial diagnostic test for a 27-year-old woman with abdominal pain and vaginal bleeding
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Obstetrics > Failed pregnancy
(Flag as important
A 27-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with vaginal bleeding and lower
abdominal pain. She had her last period six weeks ago. She has irregular periods, each lasting
variably between 4 and 7 days. On examination, her blood pressure is 110/75 mmHg, pulse
rate 98 bpm, and respiratory rate 18 breaths per minute. The rest of the exam is inconclusive.
