Question ID 189
Title Choice of contraception for a 24-year-old woman on carbamazepine
Category Obstetrics / Gynecology > Gynecology > Contraception
(Flag as important Notes
A 24-year-old woman is at your office for a prescription for oral contraceptive pills. She has
a history of epilepsy for the past five years and is on carbamazepine. She has not had any
episodes of seizures in the past six months. Which one of the following would be the most
